# global ignore file for fd. fd resolves this path itself ($XDG_CONFIG_HOME/fd/ignore) — no
# environment variable is involved, unlike ripgrep's RIPGREP_CONFIG_PATH.
#
# .gitignore syntax. lowest precedence of fd's ignore sources, so a project's own .gitignore,
# .ignore or .fdignore still wins, and `fd --no-ignore` bypasses all of them.
#
# ⚠ kept deliberately in step with ~/.config/ripgrep/config. rg excluded these while fd
# descended into them, so `fd foo` and `rg foo` disagreed about what "the tree" is — the same
# search returning results from node_modules in one tool and not the other.
# ⚠ fd has no config file for *flags*, only this ignore list. rg's --hidden/--smart-case have
# no equivalent here and must be passed on the command line.

.git/

# dependency and build trees
node_modules/
.venv/
target/

# macos noise
.DS_Store
